# performance_overview.mdc — Performance Overview (Phase 2)

## Purpose
When multiple strategy instances run concurrently, the system MUST provide a population-first overview
that enables fast selection of promising candidates and fast elimination of underperformers.

The overview is a control-plane read model: portfolio view first, drill-down second.

## Phase Scope
This rule defines Phase 2 performance tracking:
- Windowed, cross-strategy aggregates (1h / 7h / 1d / 7d / all)
- Top performers categorization
- Evidence labeling (INSUFFICIENT_DATA) to avoid ranking noise
- Uses realized performance from CLOSED trades only (market resolved/closed)

No unrealized PnL, equity curves, or portfolio allocation are required in this phase.

## Core Principles (Elite Standard)
1) Population-first: the default view is all strategy instances compared side-by-side.
2) Windowed truth: comparisons must be selectable by time window.
3) Evidence before ranking: never promote/rank without minimum sample thresholds.
4) Cost realism: realized PnL MUST be net of fees (and explicitly documented).
5) One-call overview: the UI MUST NOT use N+1 calls across strategies for the overview page.

## Data Model Rules
- Performance overview MUST be derived from CLOSED trades (StrategyClosedTradeEvent equivalent).
- Each closed trade record MUST include:
  - strategy_id, execution_mode, exit_ts_wall (UTC), pnl (net), result (WIN/LOSS/BREAKEVEN)
  - optional: size, duration_seconds, market_slug (for later slicing)
- Closed trade storage MUST be queryable by time window and grouped by strategy_id.

## API Rules
The Control API MUST expose a single endpoint for overview aggregation:

GET /api/v1/state/strategies/performance/overview

Query params:
- since: ISO 8601 datetime UTC (optional; omit for "all time")
- until: ISO 8601 datetime UTC (optional; default server now())
- execution_mode: {paper, live} (optional)
- template_type_id (optional)
- state (optional: RUNNING/STOPPED/etc.)
- sort_by: {total_realized_pnl, win_rate_pct, trade_count} (optional, default total_realized_pnl desc)
- limit (optional, default 200, max 1000)

The UI constructs since/until from window presets (1h, 7h, 1d, 7d, all) client-side.

Response MUST include:
- resolved from_ts_wall / to_ts_wall timestamps in UTC (server computed)
- one row per strategy instance with aggregates for the resolved window

The endpoint MUST be implementable without requiring the trader runtime process;
it reads from persisted closed trade records and strategy registry.

## Evidence Tier Rules (Phase 2)
Each strategy row MUST include:
- evidence_tier:
  - INSUFFICIENT_DATA if trade_count < MIN_TRADES_WINDOW
  - TRACKING otherwise

MIN_TRADES_THRESHOLD MUST be configurable (env var PERF_MIN_TRADES_THRESHOLD).
Initial default: 1 (we have limited data). Raise to 10–30 as trade volume grows.

Top-performer categorization MUST ignore INSUFFICIENT_DATA rows by default.

## UI Rules
Console MUST provide a Performance Overview page:
- Window selector: 1h / 7h / 1d / 7d / all (computes since/until client-side)
- Table with sortable columns using overview endpoint only (single call)
- Top performers panel derived from the same dataset
- Drill-down link to existing per-strategy performance endpoint

## Non-Negotiables
- Do not compute “summary from page items” for overview: overview must be server-side aggregation.
- Do not require reading all trades into memory for aggregation; use DB aggregation queries.
- Do not promote strategies solely from being top in a short window; evidence tier gates apply.
